# nr-office-quality-structure: what the lead applies (all of it is in files this task does not own)

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-quality/src/lib.rs
After the line `pub mod score;` add:

    pub mod structure;

(The module is `structure/{mod,docx,pptx,xlsx}.rs`, already in the tree.)

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-quality/Cargo.toml
[dependencies]: add, after the `mixdog-ooxml = { workspace = true }` line:

    mixdog-office-design = { workspace = true }

The structure review reads the design crate's `discipline::{font_family_key, is_motif_shape, is_picture_shape}` and
`templates::annotate_pptx_snapshot_roles`, and the ooxml crate's `xlsx_formula_audit::audit_xlsx_formulas` and
`xlsx_audit_support::sheet_path` (already a dependency). mixdog-office-design and mixdog-ooxml do not depend on
mixdog-office-quality, so the edge makes no cycle. No new external crate.

## 3. native/core/Cargo.lock
Lead regenerates it offline. The package `mixdog-office-quality` gains the dependency `mixdog-office-design` (a workspace
crate already in the lock).

## 4. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json
`node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index` adds the row of the new set `office-structure`
(recorder benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-structure.mjs, 1 file, golden.json). The set's own MANIFEST.json is
already written (native/core/fixtures/office-structure/MANIFEST.json, sha256 32d488fb5127a16a5f9941593e5d864d15d61eedc684eba8d90c3ff20abfb269,
golden.json 2476411 bytes). If the row is written by hand, in "sets" after "office-snapshot-docx" or wherever "office-structure" sorts:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-structure.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-structure/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "32d488fb5127a16a5f9941593e5d864d15d61eedc684eba8d90c3ff20abfb269",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-structure.mjs",
      "set": "office-structure",
      "totalBytes": 2476411
    },

## 5. Consumers (later tasks of the track, not this one)
The office inspect and review actions (`office-actions-inspect.mjs`, the assurance benchmark) call
`mixdog_office_quality::structure::review_office_structure(format: Option<&str>, document: &Value, audit_profile: &str) -> Vec<Value>`
(`reviewOfficeStructure({ format, document, auditProfile })`; the format falls back to `document.format`; an unknown format
answers no issues). The format reviews are also public: `structure::docx::review_docx_structure(&Value)`,
`structure::pptx::review_pptx_structure(&Value, audit_profile)` and `structure::xlsx::review_xlsx_structure(&Value, audit_profile)`.
The deck review annotates a clone of the snapshot (`annotatePptxSnapshotRoles` mutates the caller's document in Node); the
caller's document is not changed.

## 6. Nothing else
No protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING name, no desktop fragment, no environment variable.
